  "text": "### Bulletin #4: Phishing Alert – Real Attempt in Branch  \n**Date Issued:** 2026-02-10\n**Effective:** Immediate\n**Audience:** All Staff  \n**Summary:**\nOn February 8, 2026, a customer arrived at London Canary Wharf branch claiming to be \"security team\" requesting customer account access to \"verify fraud.\" Suspected social engineering attack. Staff correctly declined. Alert: Fraudsters may approach branches pretending to be bank staff.  \n**Red Flags to Watch For:**\n- Visitor claims to be from bank wanting account access\n- Caller claims to be from Head Office requesting staff credentials\n- Email from \"senior management\" asking for customer list\n- Customer reports suspicious phone call claiming to verify transactions  \n**What to Do:**\n- Verify identity by calling back using known number (not number provided)\n- Never share customer data without proper authorization\n- Never share staff login credentials\n- Report suspicious activity immediately to manager  \n**Report To:**\n- Security Alert email: security@firstuk.bank\n- If urgent: Manager immediately + 0800-555-SECURITY  \n---",
